==================== Input ====================
// `responses`, `schemas` and `properties` order their children, never their own entries.
//
// The status codes keep source order. Each child is ordered by the response table, and the keys are
// chosen so the two candidate tables disagree:
//   responses table [description, headers, content, links] -> content, links, type
//   properties table [description, type, items, ...]       -> type, content, links
//
// `properties.content` then shows the precedence: `content` has its own (empty) table, and that beats
// the properties table its parent would have applied, so it comes out alphabetically.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "x": {
    "responses": {
      "404": { "links": {}, "type": "t", "content": {} },
      "200": { "type": "t", "content": {}, "links": {} },
      "properties": { "links": {}, "type": "t", "content": { "format": "f", "type": "t", "description": "d" } }
    }
  }
}

==================== Output ====================
